# Advertek Agent Rail

This project is an MCP server and REST API that lets AI agents order print
production from Advertek, including offset, digital, wide-format, packaging,
print-on-demand, and direct-mail jobs. Orders are paid in USDC on Solana.

## Stack

- Use TypeScript and Node.js.
- Use `@modelcontextprotocol/sdk` for the MCP server.
- Use `@solana/web3.js` and `@solana/spl-token` for payments.
- Use QuickNode as the Solana RPC provider. Read its endpoint from
  `QUICKNODE_RPC_URL`; never hardcode it.
- Use OKX REST API v5 for treasury sweeps and fiat settlement.
- Validate every external input, including agent specifications and webhook
  payloads, with Zod.

## Conventions

- Never put secrets, private keys, or API keys in code. Load all secrets from
  environment variables through one centralized config module.
- Add an explicit unit test for every payment-related function before treating
  it as complete.
- Prefer small, single-purpose modules over large files.
- Represent all monetary amounts as integers in their smallest unit, such as
  lamports or USDC base units. Never use floating-point values for money.
